ided to make the story animated you  could have done a traditional  documentary  talk to us about that decision and what  it allowed you to do  one thing was that he wanted to be  anonymous because what he did what you  hear in the film is his real voice  telling the story for the very first  time and it's not easy for him to talk  about so the fact that he could be  anonymous and didn't have to be in the  public eye with the story was was really  what enabled him to start to open up  but then it's also  you know because most of the story takes  place in the past so  how do you make the past come back alive  and here animation was really good tool  to do that but and also you know sort of  the audience sees this family struggle  to get money to safely travel to a new  country while also evading law  enforcement and i just thought wow that  is that is happening today right now as  we speak and it sort of really  crystallized for me the struggle and the  plight that people who just want a  better life what they have to go through  to get that life and  we should just be a little bit more  accommodating in understanding that yeah  definitely and and you know in the  beginning this project is really born  from the friendship and my curiosity  about about my friend but then seeing  what's going on now you know i really  hoped that because this story is sold  from the inside of our friendship that i  gave some new ones to these kind of  refugee stories so you could see that  yes he's a refugee but he's so much more  you know he also has hopes and dreams  and ambitions like everyone else yeah  and so we're hearing his regular voice  but in the animation he's laying down  was that a deliberate technique that you  used it is  i have a background in radio uh and when  you do radio of course you don't have an  image so by having him lay down and  close his eyes and talk present sense  it's really a way of making be really  descriptive and and and you get the  sense of presence into his way of  talking in another way how are you  processing that you're nominated for  three oscars from this story that you're  just telling a story about your friend  did that surprise you  you didn't start out thinking i'm gonna  or maybe you did think i'm gonna go for  an oscar here no no no no you know it's  it's it started out a conversation  between me and him just the two of us in  my living room in copenhagen you know  and then from there i just grew and grew  and it's been now it's almost a decade  since we started and and to be here now  and being nominated for three academy  awards is just so it's unreal can i just  ask you about the technique like the  idea of like making it an animated film  but there are scenes where you're using  file footage from afghanistan which when  the first time that happens i thought  wow this is so cool like what made you i  did two players did you think the same  yeah  what made you decide to pick that route  no but i just wanted to make sure that  people understood that this is a real  story that underneath the animation you  have a real person and a real voice to  keep so to keep this authenticity to  have this alcohol footage in there to  kind of remind people that this is a  real story and the reason why he had to  flee is because of historical events  that happened in the world we all belong  to so i wanted to have that throughout  the film you also lay on the layer that  he's gay which was also a very difficult  time for him because in his family  you didn't talk about it in afghanistan  so he has to tell him yeah yeah he had  to tell that part of the story too and  there's some humor that you also use  yeah but i think you know again to kind  of show you know the nuance of it that  that he's a regular person who also  falls in love who also is attracted to  to he's attracted to chocolate fandam  you know there's these kind of light  moments in the film and it's so  important to get that so you see the  nuance of it and you see that refugees  are not just refugees you know they do  they're human beings regular people  we're all we are all descended from  migrants if not migrants ourselves i  mean it's funny how quickly we forget  that yeah we need a movie like this to  remind us yeah  bravo well done well done i can't wait  for the academy awards cheering cheering  you on big time jonas poe rasmussen we  thank you again flea is currently in  select theaters and you can watch in the  comfort in your home of your home it's  streaming on hulu very easy to find it
 

